<div class="top"><h3>Individual occupational therapy</h3><div class="price">{{ site.services[0].priceLabel }}</div></div>
<p>One-hour sessions built around the everyday activities your child is working toward — eating, dressing, playing, managing big feelings, joining in.</p>
<ul>
<li>In your home, or out in the community where the activity happens</li>
<li>Goals set with you in the first session, and revisited as your child changes</li>
<li>You're part of the session rather than waiting outside it</li>
<li>I can join your child during community programs — a gymnastics class, swim lessons, an after-school activity — whenever the provider is happy to have me along</li>
</ul>
<p class="caveat">Any additional cost for me to take part in a community program is covered by the family.</p>
</div>

<div class="svc">
<div class="top"><h3>Parent &amp; family consulting</h3><div class="price">{{ site.services[1].priceLabel }}</div></div>
<p>Individualized support for you, whether or not your child is taking part in OT sessions themselves.</p>
<ul>
<li>Strategies for what's often called behavior — what's driving it and what need it's meeting</li>
<li>Coping-skill development, for your child and for the adults around them</li>
<li>Practical ways to grow participation in daily activities: dressing, showering, eating, chores</li>
<li>Home set-up and safety</li>
</ul>
<p class="caveat">A genuine option when a child isn't up for sessions right now, or when the most useful change is one the adults can make.</p>
